INT. GRAND HOTEL - PENTHOUSE SUITE - NIGHT

Gilded mirrors. A white piano. A cocktail cabinet inlaid with mother-of-pearl. French windows open on a balcony, and beyond it a city of lights.

A figure in a tuxedo and a domino mask kneels at a wall safe behind a painting, working a stethoscope against its steel face. He is lean, gloved, silent.

The doorknob turns. He freezes. The painting drops back over the safe. He slides behind a velvet curtain.

A woman enters: GENEVIEVE MONTAGUE-OSEI (50s, evening gown, a glass of champagne in one hand). She flicks on a lamp. She sets down her glass on the piano. She crosses to the painting. Adjusts it by a half inch.

GENEVIEVE
(without turning)
You may come out. I can smell the rubber.

The curtain stirs. The MASKED MAN steps out, hands raised, glove squeaking.

MASKED MAN
Madame.

GENEVIEVE
Your name.

MASKED MAN
That would be unwise.

GENEVIEVE
Then I shall call you Monsieur Curtain.

MASKED MAN
Charming.

She lifts the champagne, sips, studies him over the rim.

GENEVIEVE
You are very good. The alarm is quiet.

MASKED MAN
I had help.

GENEVIEVE
The bellhop?

MASKED MAN
The night manager.

GENEVIEVE
Ah. Lucien. He has always been lazy.

She walks around him in a slow circle. He turns to follow. They halt, face to face, close enough to touch.

GENEVIEVE (CONT'D)
What is it you want?

MASKED MAN
Nothing that belongs to you.

GENEVIEVE
Everything in this room belongs to me.

MASKED MAN
Not the diamonds.

GENEVIEVE
(smiling)
Ah. You know about the diamonds.

MASKED MAN
I know they're not real.

The smile fades. A beat. Then he lunges for the painting; she smashes her glass against the piano and slashes at him with the stem. He ducks, spins, wrenches the painting down. She grabs his arm. They stagger, crash into the cocktail cabinet, and bottles shatter.

He gets the painting. She gets the mask. It tears away. Beneath it: the face of a man in his sixties, lined, gentle. LUCIEN FAIRWEATHER-ODUYA, the night manager, panting.

GENEVIEVE (CONT'D)
(whispering)
Lucien.

LUCIEN
Genevieve.

GENEVIEVE
You said you would never.

LUCIEN
You said the diamonds were real.

They stand, ruined, among the glass.
